Yes, Quest monster generation does not respect extinction.

But let me clarify what I was suggesting:

A no-input-required method of letting a summoner create tens of
thousands of nasties - with no risk to you, letting your pet army -
consisting of Archons and purple worms - slaughter everything with no
input required, and coming through afterward to collect the death
drops and harvest the polyfodder.  Note that there is a risk that an
Umber hulk could confuse your worms and trick them into killing your
Archons.

Playing an extinctionist is generally extremely boring - casting
'create monster' like crazy, and letting your pets kill everything.
As you noted earlier, sacrificing most of the kills will give you the
following benefits: artifact gifts, divine protection, HP boosts, and
piles of spellbooks.  But really, it isn't worth the extra boredom, at
least for most of the game.  The HP boosts can be MUCH more easily
obtained through alchemy, the spells can easily be obtained through
polypiling.

The major benefit of conducting a sacfest that you generally can't get
through a summoner-induced slaughter is the -128 AC that you might
want.  That is usually obtained through pudding farming, rather than
'create monster'


